{
  "name": "turn",
  "entity_kind": "process",
  "context": "A turn runs to completion on the server once started, and its full event stream is durably observable, independent of any client connection. Closing/dropping the originating connection detaches; it never cancels the turn or kills the provider. The complete turn stream is published to the per-session presence-event ring, so it can be replayed to a reconnecting client and observed live by any other attached surface. A client reconnecting mid-turn resumes from a cursor; on turn completion it sees the final result even if no client was attached when the turn finished. The turn result is persisted to session history exactly as today. Turns remain bounded and cancellable without a connection: a hung provider, a closed session, or server shutdown can stop a detached turn promptly."
}

